From: jomon <jomon@local>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] platform/x86: toshiba_acpi: add DNBK0001 to the ACPI match table

Dynabook is the spun-off Toshiba PC division. Its firmware still implements
the Toshiba HCI/SCI protocol verbatim, under ACPI device \_SB.VALZ with
_HID "DNBK0001". The in-tree toshiba_acpi driver implements this exact
protocol but its ACPI match table only lists Toshiba-era IDs, so it never
binds on Dynabook hardware.

Without the driver bound, the EC hotkey FIFO is never drained and no events
reach Linux: there is no keyboard-backlight device in /sys/class/leds and the
Fn brightness / keyboard-backlight keys produce no usable events (the panel
backlight itself works independently).

Add DNBK0001 to the match table so the driver attaches and exposes the
hardware. Tested on a Dynabook Portege X40-K.

Signed-off-by: jomon <jomon@local>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c b/drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c
@@ -241,6 +241,7 @@ static const struct acpi_device_id toshiba_device_ids[] = {
 	{"TOS6200", 0},
 	{"TOS6207", 0},
 	{"TOS6208", 0},
 	{"TOS1900", 0},
+	{"DNBK0001", 0},	/* dynabook (Portege X40-K etc.) rebranded TOS1900 */
 	{"", 0},
 };
